      "page_content": "1. Purpose\nThis policy defines approval authority levels for booking Order Intake and establishes requirements for Order Backlog\nmonitoring.\n2. Scope\nApplies to all Orders booked as Order Intake and to periodic review of Order Backlog balances.\n3. Approval Authority Matrix\nOrder Value | Approver\nUp to $50,000 | Sales Manager\n$50,001 – $250,000 | Regional Finance Head\nAbove $250,000 | CFO\nApproval must be documented and retained in the order file.\n4. Order Backlog Management\n4.1 Review Frequency\nOrder Backlog is reviewed on a quarterly basis by the Finance team.\n4.2 Aging Calculation\nAging (Days) = Current Date - Original Order Booking Date\n4.3 Flagging Criteria\nBacklog items shall be flagged for review when:\n- Aging (Days) > 365 days (12 months), AND\n- No delivery milestone has been recorded in the system\nFlagged items require Finance Manager review to determine whether continued recognition remains appropriate.\n5. Roles and Responsibilities\nRole | Responsibility\nSales Manager | Approves orders up to $50,000\nRegional Finance Head | Approves orders $50,001–$250,000\nCFO | Approves orders above $250,000\nFinance Team | Performs quarterly Backlog review\n6. Related Policies\n- POL-ORD-001: Order Intake Recognition & Measurement Policy\nCFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | CONTROLLED DOCUMENT Page 2",
      "metadata": {
        "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-003_v1.0_Order-Intake-Approval-Backlog-Management.pdf",
